{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_authorization_gate_ladder", "label": "The authorization gate ladder (rungs 0-7)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "## The order", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A call has to survive all of them, in a fixed order, and none can grant what an earlier one withheld. Derived from Agent::run_one_tool and Agent::dispatch_tool, not from prose."}, {"id": "docs_authorization_name_interception", "label": "Rung 1: name interception", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "### 1. Name interception", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ask_user, write_tasks and task return before the class is looked up. task is exempt because its child is constrained, not because delegation is inherently harmless."}, {"id": "docs_authorization_plan_gated", "label": "Rung 2: plan_gated (no bypass)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "### 2. plan_gated", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The one gate in the system with no bypass at all, and the reason the order matters: every later rung is written on the assumption that this one already ran."}, {"id": "docs_authorization_needs_prompt", "label": "Rung 4: needs_prompt (four sufficient exemptions)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "### 4. Whether to ask at all", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four independent reasons not to prompt OR'd together; none is stronger than another, which is the source of most of the surprising cases."}, {"id": "docs_authorization_concurrent_path", "label": "The concurrent read-only path (run_concurrent_group)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "### The concurrent path", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rungs 2, 4 and 5 are skipped entirely; sound only because is_concurrency_safe admits nothing but exactly ReadOnly tools. Anything added to rungs 2-5 must be added to both paths or explicitly argued not to apply."}, {"id": "docs_authorization_pretooluse_position", "label": "Why PreToolUse sits at rung 3", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "## Where PreToolUse sits, and why", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Above the plan gate it would fire for calls that cannot execute and invite being wired as an override; below the prompt it could not prevent the prompt and a rewrite would produce a confused deputy. Above rung 4 specifically so it still runs under /permission skip."}, {"id": "docs_authorization_finding_a_readset_laundering", "label": "Finding A: a subagent's reads unlocked the parent's overwrites", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "### A.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fixed by splitting identities: ToolContext carries session_id for on-disk state and reader_id for what has been read, because session_id also names staging, scratch and the checkpoint stream /rewind walks."}, {"id": "docs_authorization_finding_b_allowed_tools", "label": "Finding B: --allowed-tools is not deny-by-default", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "### B.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "headless.rs answers the permission channel, so a call that never reaches the channel is never checked against the flag. Fixed for the two cases that mattered via with_unattended; the accurate statement is that nothing that writes, runs a command, or spawns an agent happens without it."}, {"id": "docs_authorization_finding_c_schema_check", "label": "Finding C: three tools were never schema-checked", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "### C.", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fixed by validating the intercepted three against the published schema before interception; the list lives in one constant, INTERCEPTED_TOOLS, because two things have to agree about it."}, {"id": "docs_authorization_class_is_authority", "label": "A read-only tool is not a harmless tool", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "## Where two of them disagree", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "web_search reaches the network and task spawns a whole agent; web_fetch is Mutating despite writing nothing because a model-chosen URL is an exfiltration primitive. The class is about authority, not about whether bytes hit the disk."}, {"id": "docs_authorization_session_grant_outranks_policy", "label": "A session grant outranks a tightened policy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "## Where two of them disagree", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "allowed_session_tools is checked before permission_policy and set_permission_policy does not clear grants, so 'the policy is ask' is not the same claim as 'you will be asked'."}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_provider_model_switching", "target": "claude_unattended_mode", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "Carried across /model alongside the limits and the redactor", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "agents_redaction_choke_point", "target": "docs_authorization_gate_ladder", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "PostToolUse hook -> redact -> result", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_authorization_gate_ladder", "target": "docs_authorization_name_interception", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "rung 1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_authorization_gate_ladder", "target": "docs_authorization_plan_gated", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "rung 2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_authorization_gate_ladder", "target": "docs_hooks_pretooluse", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "rung 3", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_authorization_gate_ladder", "target": "docs_authorization_needs_prompt", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "rung 4", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_authorization_gate_ladder", "target": "docs_authorization_concurrent_path", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "### The concurrent path", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_authorization_pretooluse_position", "target": "docs_hooks_pretooluse", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "## Where PreToolUse sits, and why", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_authorization_plan_gated", "target": "claude_plan_gate", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/authorization.md", "source_location": "### 2. plan_gated", "weight": 1.0}, {"sou